{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator-documentation AC extended during epic e369's plan review. `docs/user-guide.md` must now state:\n\n- the DC **least-privilege** expectation — a dedicated service account whose PAT is scoped to only the reconciled projects (Browse Projects / Create Issues / Edit Issues / Add Comments / Link Issues), never an admin token;\n- `allow_insecure` as cleartext-only-if-you-must;\n- the **`ca_bundle`** key for internal-CA certificates;\n- **`resolved_statuses`** for workflows that do not use the conventional Resolved/Done/Cancelled state names.\n\nThe ADR should also record what the epic settled: the Jira-family sub-seam is shared by **dependency inversion** for ADR 0035 §(a)'s location-pinned modules (`adf.py`, `outbound_fields.py`, `comment_limits.py` keep their paths; only their contents change to import from `jira_family/`), because relocating them is ADR 0035 **Phase 2**'s work. Note also that `deleted -> Done` was unified in J2 as a deliberate, declared behavior fix, and that `rebar_reconciler/config.py`'s third copy of the status map is left to bug `fe15-3bc4-ed70-4b61`.\n\nBlocked by J7."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338342992192001,"uuid":"66507915-82f5-4227-8260-afc1ef5030d5"}